---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const faqSchema = {
 "@context": "https://schema.org",
 "@type": "FAQPage",
 "mainEntity": [
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "What is remove from spamhaus blocklist in simple terms?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Think of it as the rulebook that a specific part of the internet follows. Every page in this section explains one rule, why it exists, and how to follow it correctly."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Do I need to memorize all of this?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "No: bookmark this page and the related tools. The goal is understanding what to check and when, not memorizing syntax."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "How long does it take to implement?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Most configurations take 5-15 minutes in your DNS panel. The verification (using our tools) takes another 2 minutes."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "What happens if I get it wrong?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Depends on the setting: some errors cause immediate visible failures, others silently degrade deliverability or security. Every guide includes the symptoms to watch for."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Is this the same across all DNS providers?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "The underlying protocol is identical; the dashboard layout and terminology differ. Our provider playbooks cover the exact flow for Cloudflare, GoDaddy, Namecheap, Route 53, and others."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Where can I get help if I'm stuck?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Each guide links to the relevant free tool so you can verify your work. The support page lists email channels for questions the guides don't cover."
   }
  }
 ]
}
---
<BaseLayout title="How to Get Off the Spamhaus Blocklist (SBL, XBL, PBL)"  description="Spamhaus delisting guide: identify which Spamhaus list you are on, fix the root cause, and request removal the right way."  schema={[faqSchema]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/email-authentication/" class="hover:text-accent">Email Authentication</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/email-deliverability/" class="hover:text-accent">Email Deliverability</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">Spamhaus Removal</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">How to Get Off the Spamhaus Blocklist</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">
      Spamhaus operates several lists with different meanings and different cures. Half of all
      delisting pain comes from treating them as one thing. Identify yours first, fix the cause,
      then request removal.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-8 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60">
      <table class="pdns-table">
        <thead><tr><th>List</th><th>Why you are on it</th><th>The fix</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td class="font-mono text-xs text-accent">SBL</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Spam operations, phishing, malware associated with your IP or domain.</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Remove the malicious content/compromise, then contact Spamhaus with evidence.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="font-mono text-xs text-accent">XBL / CSS</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Your IP shows exploit or open-proxy behavior.</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Clean the server, close the proxy, request re-scan.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="font-mono text-xs text-accent">PBL</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Your IP is in dynamic/residential space that should not send direct mail.</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Send through your ISP's smarthost or a provider; or use the PBL removal form if genuinely static.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="font-mono text-xs text-accent">DBL (domain)</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Your domain appeared in spam payloads.</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Stop the campaign/compromise sending it, then request DBL removal.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="rich-text mt-10">
      <h2>The procedure</h2>
      <ol class="list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-5">
        <li><strong>Look up your IP or domain</strong> in the Spamhaus lookup (zen.spamhaus.org returns codes telling you which list fired). Our <a href="/blacklist-checker/">blacklist checker</a> gives an honest first pass, with the caveat that Spamhaus refuses public-resolver queries.</li>
        <li><strong>Fix the root cause completely.</strong> Compromised account, open redirect, misconfigured server, abused form: the listing returns if you only request removal.</li>
        <li><strong>Request removal</strong> through the Spamhaus form for your list. Free for small volumes; include what happened and what changed.</li>
        <li><strong>Watch propagation.</strong> Delisting flows to users of the data within hours; some filters cache longer.</li>
      </ol>
      <h2>Preventing the encore</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Authenticate (SPF, DKIM, <a href="/dmarc/">DMARC</a>) so compromise is visible in reports, not discovered via listings.</li>
        <li>Monitor: re-run the <a href="/blacklist-checker/">blacklist checker</a> weekly, or let <a href="/pricing/">monitoring</a> do it.</li>
      </ul>
      
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What is remove from spamhaus blocklist in simple terms?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Think of it as the rulebook that a specific part of the internet follows. Every page in this section explains one rule, why it exists, and how to follow it correctly.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Do I need to memorize all of this?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">No: bookmark this page and the related tools. The goal is understanding what to check and when, not memorizing syntax.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How long does it take to implement?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Most configurations take 5-15 minutes in your DNS panel. The verification (using our tools) takes another 2 minutes.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What happens if I get it wrong?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Depends on the setting: some errors cause immediate visible failures, others silently degrade deliverability or security. Every guide includes the symptoms to watch for.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Is this the same across all DNS providers?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">The underlying protocol is identical; the dashboard layout and terminology differ. Our provider playbooks cover the exact flow for Cloudflare, GoDaddy, Namecheap, Route 53, and others.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Where can I get help if I'm stuck?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Each guide links to the relevant free tool so you can verify your work. The support page lists email channels for questions the guides don't cover.</p></details></div>
<h2>Related</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/get-off-barracuda-blocklist/">Barracuda delisting</a> and <a href="/sorbs-delisting-guide/">SORBS delisting</a></li>
        <li><a href="/why-emails-go-to-spam/">Why emails go to spam</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
